{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 1 RCA (pre-fix):\n\nStep 0(a): duplicate sweep found this bug (`pathworky-unrivaled-firefly`) plus the ops ledger that discovered it; prior closed c943 is a related LLM-Review voter precedent, not a duplicate of the CI Verified workflow.\nStep 0(b): no version field; report created_at 1788369753410902832 maps to `origin/main` floor 952f0825321c755f41edce412ad1fe9f1db9268d. The suspect workflow line range has not changed since that floor.\nStep 0(c): fresh worktree `/Users/joeoakhart/debug-adab-closed-vote` is at 952f0825321c755f41edce412ad1fe9f1db9268d (= `origin/main`).\n\nObserved mechanism: `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml` final `vote` job step `Cast Verified from the CI conclusion` delegates directly to `lfreleng-actions/gerrit-review-action` (lines 504-523 on the working tree). The representative run log for 33580445347 shows the workflow conclusion normalized to `vote-type='success'`, then the action shell ran `ssh ... gerrit review 2483,7 ...`, Gerrit returned `error: fatal: change is closed` / `fatal: one or more reviews failed`, and GitHub failed the step with exit code 1. That proves the runtime path treats every nonzero `gerrit review` as a red CI failure, including the closed-change race.\n\nAuthoritative intent / design-decision check: ADR 0020/0023 require CI to cast `Verified` independently and fail closed when the SSH vote cannot be cast on an open/voteable change. They do not require a red run after the target change has already become unvoteable. Closed precedent c943 records that Gerrit `409` / `change is closed` for a merged/abandoned change is terminal/non-actionable for the LLM-Review voter. No ADR found that forbids treating a closed/abandoned/merged vote-time race as a benign no-op.\n\nConfirmed root cause: the final CI Verified cast is implemented as an opaque third-party action invocation with no wrapper around the `gerrit review` exit status, so the workflow has no branch that can classify Gerrit's specific `fatal: change is closed` response as terminal/no-op while preserving failures for open changes.\n\nDefect legitimacy: defect. It violates the ticket AC and the two-vote gate's intent: CI result should vote when the change is voteable; a change that has already been abandoned/merged cannot receive a vote and should not make an otherwise successful gate run red.\n\nAttribution: scope-of-work omission in the original two-vote Verified gate implementation, commit 49ad69bcd242cfa7969331fc813805432072d791 (`feat: CI as a second Gerrit gate vote (Verified) via gerrit-to-platform`, epic/story family 1fa8). Blame/log -L on the final cast step shows the direct action invocation was introduced there; later commits only normalized inputs or comments/pins and did not add/remove a closed-change handler. I will recover the exact origin ticket id for `--caused-by` before close.\n\nFix plan: add a small trusted helper `scripts/cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py`, sparse-check it out in the vote job, and replace only the final cast action with a shell step that installs the same SSH material, runs `gerrit review`, exits 0 with a clear notice only when Gerrit's output contains `fatal: change is closed`, and returns the original nonzero code for every other vote failure. Keep the clear-vote start step unchanged. Add script tests for closed-change RED/GREEN, other failures, success command shape, and validation; update existing workflow structural tests to pin the final cast helper boundary."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788370798292325994,"uuid":"1a7c33c3-10d3-4ae7-aabd-b6d80d088228"}